      "name": "Strathclyde Transport Development Study (1988)",
      "status": "abandoned",
      "description": "Strathclyde PTE's 1988 study looked at Subway extensions north from Hillhead and Kelvinbridge via Kirklee and Maryhill to Summerston, west from Govan to Glasgow Airport, and an eastern city-centre loop via High Street and Gorbals Cross; it concluded that extending the Subway was not warranted.",
