    "halcrow-1954": {
      "name": "Halcrow Report (1954)",
      "status": "abandoned",
      "description": "Sir William Halcrow & Partners' 1954 report proposed taking the Subway south from Glasgow Cross to Castlemilk and north from Glasgow Cross through Anderston to an interchange at Partick Cross, then to Kelvindale, Blairdardie and Drumchapel, partly in disused railway tunnels and partly on the surface. Not pursued, mainly for lack of funds.",
